    "category": "Satan and spiritual beings",
    "myth": "The devil lives in hell and rules it, tormenting people there.",
    "truth": "Scripture never shows the devil ruling hell. It was prepared as a place of judgment <em>for</em> the devil and his angels, not a kingdom for him. In Scripture he roams the earth, and Jesus now holds the keys of death and the grave.",
    "detail": "The book argues that the image of a devil reigning in hell owes more to Dante's poem, Milton's play-like epic and medieval ideas (it even suggests influence from the Islamic story of Muhammad's night journey) than to the Bible. The words behind “hell” are Sheol and Hades (the grave) and Gehenna, the Valley of Hinnom just outside Jerusalem. In Job, Satan comes from roaming the earth. Peter pictures him prowling like a lion. Ephesians calls him the prince of the power of the air. Hebrews 2:14 says Jesus, by his death, rendered powerless the one who had the power of death. On most traditional readings of Revelation 20, the devil, death and Hades will later be thrown into the lake of fire, though some think this was fulfilled in AD 70.",
