    "truth": "The devil is a created being. He is not God's equal opposite, and he can only be in one place at a time. Most troubles blamed on him come from wrong choices, wrong thinking, believing lies or, at most, some lesser spirit, not from Satan personally.",
    "detail": "On his travels the author has met many sincere people who said the devil was attacking their family, money or health. He kindly tells them that this is very unlikely. Only God is omnipresent. The book jokes that Satan is not like the Santa of the Christmas song, who watches everyone all the time. Job says the adversary roams and walks the earth, which he would not need to do if he were already everywhere. 1 Peter says he looks for someone he <em>may</em> devour, which implies he needs an open door. Even the archangel Michael is not everywhere at once. The church has given a defeated devil far too much credit. Often our greatest enemy is ourselves, as the famous line about meeting the enemy and finding it is us suggests.",
