    "detail": "The disciples' question in Matthew 24:3 asked about the end of the <em>age</em>, as most modern translations render it, and the same applies to the harvest at the end of the age in Matthew 13:39 and 49. Ephesians 3:21's “world without end” really means “age without end”. Ecclesiastes 1:4 says the earth abides forever. Psalms 78:69, 93:1 and 96:10 say the world is firmly established and will not be moved. The Hebrew <em>olam</em> means long duration or the ages. Even 2 Peter 3, read literally, ends with unrighteousness purged and the earth cleansed, not erased. Jewish thought speaks of <em>tikkun olam</em>, the repair of the world. The world will end <em>for</em> each of us when we die, but we need not live in fear. We should get busy with the Father's renovation project, which began at the cross and resurrection.",
    "scripture": "Matthew 24:3; Matthew 13:39, 49; Ephesians 3:21; Ecclesiastes 1:4; Psalm 78:69; Psalm 93:1; Psalm 96:10; Isaiah 45:17; 2 Peter 3:10-13",
