    "detail": "Popular books and films like <em>Left Behind</em> made the evacuation idea famous. The book says it can leave Christians hoping things get worse so they can be taken away, and that it breeds fear. The main proof text, 1 Thessalonians 4:17, speaks of being caught up (<em>harpazo</em>, to seize or snatch) to meet the Lord, but not of leaving. Jesus prayed in John 17:15 that the Father would <em>not</em> take his followers out of the world, so the book asks whose prayer is likely to be answered. In Noah's flood and in the parable of the wheat and tares it is the wicked who are taken and the righteous who remain. Many texts say the righteous will never be removed and the meek inherit the earth. The author says he has repeatedly challenged experts to show him otherwise. Jesus came to save the world, not to rescue people out of it, so we should carry on his business until he comes.",
