    "detail": "The conversation runs from the end of John 9 into John 10:1-12. Jesus elsewhere calls the temple leaders robbers who turned God's house into a den of thieves, accuses them of devouring widows' houses, and warns of wolves in sheep's clothing. These self-appointed shepherds treated the flock as a job and scattered it. The book grants that stealing, killing and destroying are certainly the devil's fruit and could be applied to him as a metaphor. But good interpretation first asks who the original audience was and what it meant to them, and only then applies it to us. In Jesus there is only light, life and love.",
