    "truth": "The words “and fasting” in Mark 9:29 are missing from most modern translations such as the NASB and ESV, and the point of the story is unbelief. Jesus rebukes an unbelieving generation and says all things are possible to the one who believes.",
    "detail": "The disciples already had authority over demons but could not deal with this one, and Jesus did so easily. When they asked why, the context shows the issue was their unbelief, not an unusually powerful demon. Prayer builds faith and removes unbelief, so believers can exercise the authority Christ has given them with confidence (compare Jude 20, building yourselves up in faith and praying in the Spirit). Fasting is a good discipline but is not required to cast out a demon. What is required is believing in the authority Christ has freely given.",
