    "truth": "The phrase is half a verse. Jesus says that if you continue in his word you will <em>know</em> the truth, and that truth sets you free. The knowing he means is experiential, and truth frees us when we live it out, not just when we hear it.",
    "detail": "The Greek word for know points to experience and to truth made real in life. Paul warned of people always learning but never coming to knowledge of the truth. Hearers who are not doers build on sand. Ignorance is not bliss, since God's people are destroyed for lack of knowledge, but information alone is not freedom either. Prayer lines, conference prophecies and books on freedom are good, yet without acting on them no fruit appears. Perhaps that is why Jesus washed the disciples' feet: he cared most about their walk.",
