    "myth": "Giving ten percent of your income to the church unlocks the Malachi 3 blessing and lifts the curse.",
    "truth": "Malachi speaks of the whole tithe and offerings, plural. Under the Law these added up to well over twenty percent, perhaps 23 to 30 percent depending on the scholar. Ten percent was never what activated the Malachi promise. The book deliberately does not take a side on whether tithing applies today.",
    "detail": "Israel's giving included first fruits and <em>terumah</em> (heave offerings) for the priests. There was the Levitical tithe of produce and herds (Lev 27:30-32). There was a festival tithe that families used themselves to travel to Jerusalem and feast before the Lord, which could even be turned into money and spent on food and strong drink (Deut 14:22-27). Every third year a tithe went to the Levite, the foreigner, the orphan and the widow (Deut 14:28-29). On top of these were offerings and temple taxes. Teaching that a tenth of income meets Malachi 3 leaves out that plural.",
