    "kind": "Myth",
    "category": "Words and translation",
    "myth": "Revelation 22:18-19 warns that anyone who adds to or takes from the Bible will be cursed.",
    "truth": "John was speaking specifically of the book of Revelation, the words of “this book of prophecy”. The Bible had not yet been compiled, and it is a library of books, not a single book.",
    "detail": "John borrows language from Deuteronomy 4:2 and 12:32, where Israel was told not to add to or subtract from God's commands. By Jesus' day the scribes and Pharisees had done exactly that, adding many extra rules and prohibitions. Jesus said their traditions made God's word of no effect. And if the warning covered the whole Bible, the book jokes, Protestants would need to explain removing 14 books. Ironically, people add to and take away from Scripture all the time with sayings it never contains, which the author says is why he wrote the book.",
