    "id": "die-daily",
    "n": 64,
    "kind": "Myth",
    "category": "Grace and salvation",
    "myth": "The Bible tells believers to die to self daily.",
    "truth": "When Paul says “I die daily” (1 Cor 15:31) he means he faces death every day for the gospel, which is how many modern translations render it. Believers have already died with Christ once for all, so the call is to reckon ourselves dead to sin and alive to God, not to commit spiritual suicide each morning.",
    "detail": "Denying yourself and taking up your cross (following Jesus) is not the same as repeatedly killing yourself off spiritually. In 1 Corinthians 15:30 Paul says he is in danger every hour, and Romans 8:36 speaks of being put to death all day long. Romans 6 says we were baptised into his death and our old self <em>was</em> crucified. Galatians 2:20 says I <em>have been</em> crucified with Christ. Christ died to sin once for all. Our lives are hidden with Christ and bought with a price. Paul would be horrified at the self-punishing religious gymnastics done in his name. Instead, enjoy the eternal life Christ's finished work has placed in you.",
    "scripture": "1 Corinthians 15:30-31; Luke 9:23; Romans 8:36; Romans 6:3-11; Galatians 2:20; Colossians 3:3; 1 Corinthians 6:19-20",
