RG.mmClosing = [
  "The book has no separate conclusion. It ends with Myth 70, which the author deliberately kept for last because it is the one people most often react to with anger instead of discussion. Its final thought sums up the whole book: if our picture of God is less loving and merciful than we ourselves are, the picture needs correcting. God looks exactly like Jesus, who told us to love our enemies.",
  "Throughout, the author returns to the same invitation. Do not believe something only because someone you love taught it. Check it in context and in the original languages. Hold debated matters loosely, and keep Jesus and the finished work of the New Covenant at the centre. He says repeatedly that he would rather be proved wrong and change his mind than defend a tradition. He closes many entries with a warm, humorous call to stop living in fear, whether of the devil, the end of the world, judgment or losing your salvation, and to join in the Father's renovation project of bringing heaven's life to earth."
];
